{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470897-extended-test-question-breaking-a-cipher-by-hand","id":1470897,"title":"Extended Test Question - Breaking a Cipher by Hand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-19T17:50:58-08:00","id":1470897,"title":"Extended Test Question - Breaking a Cipher by Hand","content":"Regarding a standard extended test, I'm looking for suggestions for the difficulty (accumulated successes needed) and time increment per roll to decipher some 400 letters written using a cipher between two Lasombra (Narses and Alfonzo of Venice) over the course of 19 years. A PC has hired a Nosferatu to decipher these letters because they believe they contain information regarding Narses' plot against Constantinople and want to use the letters as evidence. They currently don't know what cipher was used, but through much trial and error, the Nosferatu believes they can eventually decipher the letters by hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T12:50:06-08:00","id":1470941,"title":"","content":"If this is an NPC, just wait 40 days in game (or literally just a week if they have a computer) and hand the deciphered thing to the players. If this is a PC, roll <b>Intelligence + Investigation or Academics</b> and require a number of successes equal to 5 x one of the modifiers listed below:<ul><li>1 = Routine</li> <li>2 = Straightforward</li> <li>3 = Moderate</li> <li>4 = Challenging</li> <li>5 = Hard</li> <li>6 = Very Hard</li> <li>7 = Almost Impossible</li> </ul>Originally typed out a whole thing over complicating thing, but here's the jest. Deciphering anything takes a lot of time without a computer. Each test should take like <b>4 hours</b> to do by hand. A computer can cut this time to like an hour. Not only that, but to write down the deciphered message would take several nights, not accounting for a mistake.<br /> <br /> If this is V20, the Difficulty is 7 or 8. If this is V5 ignore this part of the message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 12-20-2021, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T13:14:32-08:00","id":1470947,"title":"","content":"Yes, the time for writing down the deciphered letters will mostly be the time to write them after the code is broken. The number of letters does not add difficulty or time to the task, it can actually make things easier as the character have more samples to compare any theory and observe patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T13:50:24-08:00","id":1470957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470897-extended-test-question-breaking-a-cipher-by-hand?p=1470947#post1470947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the time for writing down the deciphered letters will mostly be the time to write them after the code is broken. The number of letters does not add difficulty or time to the task, it can actually make things easier as the character have more samples to compare any theory and observe patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also very much true yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T03:33:16-08:00","id":1471187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470897-extended-test-question-breaking-a-cipher-by-hand#post1470897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding a standard extended test, I'm looking for suggestions for the difficulty (accumulated successes needed) and time increment per roll to decipher some 400 letters written using a cipher between two Lasombra (Narses and Alfonzo of Venice) over the course of 19 years. A PC has hired a Nosferatu to decipher these letters because they believe they contain information regarding Narses' plot against Constantinople and want to use the letters as evidence. They currently don't know what cipher was used, but through much trial and error, the Nosferatu believes they can eventually decipher the letters by hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading between the lines I'm making the assumption that you're not in the computer age for the following, if it's modern times there's advice above.<br /> <br /> Using the Dark Ages rule you're going to be making Enigmas plus Intelligence rolls - 'Medieval enigmas encompass symbolism, history, lore, and cryptography.'<br /> <br /> Depending on how fast you want it to be deciphered you could require hourly or daily rolls and anything from two to ten successes to decipher the code.<br /> <br /> Once the code is know it's merely a matter of time to plow through all 400 letters, but allow an Investigation plus Wits roll, using the same time span and a similar number of successes, to pick out the highlights, after all, not every letter will have the evidence needed.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, as the rolls aren't really necessary, you could simply say that to work it out the players need Enigmas X and Investigation Y plus up to a weeks work - it all depends on the needs of your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T10:05:02-08:00","id":1471201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470897-extended-test-question-breaking-a-cipher-by-hand?p=1471187#post1471187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading between the lines I'm making the assumption that you're not in the computer age for the following, if it's modern times there's advice above.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advice above already covered doing it by hand and assuming that the game could not be in the modern age, but you're right that Enigmas should be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T02:50:44-08:00","id":1471267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470897-extended-test-question-breaking-a-cipher-by-hand?p=1471201#post1471201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advice above already covered doing it by hand and assuming that the game could not be in the modern age, but you're right that Enigmas should be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there any real need for you to add this other than to have the last word?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}